0..73 Comment "//! Second-order rules. A rule whose right side applies a variable that a"
74..153 Comment "//! binding port of its left side binds instantiates it: `t(u)` substitutes `u`"
154..224 Comment "//! for the variable `t`\'s port binds, one argument per bound variable"
225..305 Comment "//! [Klop-1993-combinatory_reduction_systems_introduction_and_survey]. The rules"
306..360 Comment "//! terminate by the higher-order recursive path order"
361..441 Comment "//! [Jouannaud-1999-the_higher_order_recursive_path_ordering]: the instantiation"
442..522 Comment "//! is below an application that holds the variable and every argument directly."
523..603 Comment "//! A pair a second-order rule takes part in is found by pattern unification and"
604..642 Comment "//! joined in the second-order reading"
643..709 Comment "//! [Mayr-1998-higher_order_rewrite_systems_and_their_confluence]."
710..713 Comment "//!"
714..747 Comment "//! - see: #2328 — `LetOverlap`"
748..818 Comment "//! - cites: [Jouannaud-1999-the_higher_order_recursive_path_ordering]"
819..897 Comment "//! - cites: [Klop-1993-combinatory_reduction_systems_introduction_and_survey]"
